  "finalText": "## Summary\n\n**Bug:** `authService.logout(token)` called `sessionRepository.delete(token)` with the JWT, but the `sessions` table stores refresh token UUIDs — the delete matched nothing. On logout the JWT was revoked in-memory, but the refresh token persisted in the DB, so an attacker holding it could call `POST /api/auth/refresh` (no auth middleware) to mint a fresh, un-revoked access token.\n\n**Root cause trace:**\n- `authRoutes.ts:62` — extracted JWT from `Authorization` header, passed to `logout(jwt)`\n- `authService.ts:68` — `sessionRepository.delete(jwt)` → SQL `DELETE FROM sessions WHERE token = <jwt>` → 0 rows matched (sessions store UUIDs)\n- `authService.ts:72-92` — `refreshToken()` found the orphaned refresh token, issued a new JWT → full access restored\n\n**Fix (3 lines changed across 2 files):**\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/services/authService.ts:65-69` | `logout(token, userId)` now calls `sessionRepository.deleteByUserId(userId)` instead of `sessionRepository.delete(token)` — wipes all DB sessions for the user |\n| `src/routes/authRoutes.ts:61-63` | Passes `req.user.id` (already populated by `authenticate` middleware) to `authService.logout()` |\n\n**Tests added:** Two new tests in `tests/auth.test.ts`:\n1. `should delete all DB sessions for the user on logout so refresh token is invalidated` — asserts `deleteByUserId` is called with the user ID\n2. `should reject the old JWT on every protected path after logout, and refresh token is gone` — exercises `verifyToken` + `authenticate` middleware against all 22 protected paths, then asserts the DB session was destroyed",
